  "result": "The bug was an off-by-one check in `line_subtotal`. It's fixed, and all 7 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** at `shop/pricing.py:10` the code checked `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD` (threshold is 10), so the discount started at 11 units. The policy says 10 or more, so the check should be `>=`. The existing test `test_bulk_discount` already expected 10 units to get the discount, and it was failing before the fix (1083 instead of 1028).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `shop/pricing.py`: changed `>` to `>=`.\n- `tests/test_pricing.py`: added `test_no_bulk_discount_below_threshold`, which checks that 9 units get no discount. With the existing 10-unit test, both sides of the threshold are now tested.\n\nQuantities of the same item added separately are combined into one line before pricing, so a customer adding 10 units in several steps gets the discount too.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
